IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-nouns`
IMPORT `er4-part3-1-premiums-and-administration`

-- Tests of regs 76.24 to 76.3 (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1284-1319). Every expected value is written by hand from the text.
-- The amounts are invented for the tests.

§ `Reg 76.24 and 76.25 -- the premium reduction at source`

-- 76.24: covered by a provincial plan but employed in a province with no plan, or outside Canada: no reduction taken into account.
#ASSERT `reg 76.24 the employer is not to take any premium reduction into account in deducting the employee's premium or remitting the employer's premium` TRUE `er4 in a province that has no provincial plan`
#ASSERT `reg 76.24 the employer is not to take any premium reduction into account in deducting the employee's premium or remitting the employer's premium` TRUE `er4 outside Canada`
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.24 the employer is not to take any premium reduction into account in deducting the employee's premium or remitting the employer's premium` TRUE `er4 in a province that has a provincial plan`
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.24 the employer is not to take any premium reduction into account in deducting the employee's premium or remitting the employer's premium` FALSE `er4 in a province that has no provincial plan`
-- 76.25: employed in a province that has a provincial plan but not covered by it: the reduction is taken into account.
#ASSERT `reg 76.25 the employer is to take any premium reduction into account in deducting the employee's premium and remitting the employer's premium` FALSE `er4 in a province that has a provincial plan`
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.25 the employer is to take any premium reduction into account in deducting the employee's premium and remitting the employer's premium` TRUE `er4 in a province that has a provincial plan`
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.25 the employer is to take any premium reduction into account in deducting the employee's premium and remitting the employer's premium` FALSE `er4 in a province that has no provincial plan`
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.25 the employer is to take any premium reduction into account in deducting the employee's premium and remitting the employer's premium` FALSE `er4 outside Canada`

§ `Reg 76.26 -- the premium adjustment paid to the province`

-- Ruler: resides in the province on 31 December, premium reduction deducted from the person, overpayment, owed under the provincial plan, premium reduction remitted as employer's premium.
-- P1: lesser of (300 + 100 = 400) and 500 owed = 400; employer remitted 420.
`er4 test person 1` MEANS `er4 Insured person referred to in section 76.24` OF TRUE, 300, 100, 500, 420
-- P2: lesser of 200 and 150 owed = 150; employer remitted 280.
`er4 test person 2` MEANS `er4 Insured person referred to in section 76.24` OF TRUE, 200, 0, 150, 280
-- P3 lives elsewhere on 31 December: left out of both (a) and (b).
`er4 test person 3` MEANS `er4 Insured person referred to in section 76.24` OF FALSE, 999, 999, 999, 999

#ASSERT `reg 76.26(1)(a) the lesser of the total of the premium reduction deducted and the overpayment, and what the person owes under the provincial plan` `er4 test person 1` EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `reg 76.26(1)(a) the lesser of the total of the premium reduction deducted and the overpayment, and what the person owes under the provincial plan` `er4 test person 2` EQUALS 150
-- (a) = 400 + 150 = 550; (b) = 420 + 280 = 700; together 1250.
#ASSERT `reg 76.26(1)(a) the amount obtained by adding together the amounts for the insured persons who reside in the province on December 31` (LIST `er4 test person 1`, `er4 test person 2`, `er4 test person 3`) EQUALS 550
#ASSERT `reg 76.26(1)(b) the total of the premium reduction remitted by employers as employer's premiums for the insured persons who reside in the province on December 31` (LIST `er4 test person 1`, `er4 test person 2`, `er4 test person 3`) EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `reg 76.26(1) the premium adjustment that the Minister of National Revenue is to pay to the province` (LIST `er4 test person 1`, `er4 test person 2`, `er4 test person 3`) EQUALS 1250
#ASSERT `reg 76.26(1) the premium adjustment that the Minister of National Revenue is to pay to the province` (LIST `er4 test person 3`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 76.26(1) the premium adjustment that the Minister of National Revenue is to pay to the province` EMPTY EQUALS 0

§ `Reg 76.28 -- overpayment of the employee's premiums`

-- 1,200 deducted under the Act and a premium adjustment of 300 for premiums deducted under the provincial plan: 1,500 counted.
#ASSERT `reg 76.28(1) the employee's premiums taken into account in determining whether there has been an overpayment` 1200 300 EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `reg 76.28(1) the employee's premiums taken into account in determining whether there has been an overpayment` 1200 0 EQUALS 1200
-- (2): the adjustment paid to the province is not taken into account for Part IV.
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.28(2) the amount is taken into account for the purposes of Part IV of the Act` TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 76.28(2) the amount is taken into account for the purposes of Part IV of the Act` FALSE

§ `Reg 76.29 and 76.3 -- social insurance number and disclosure`

#ASSERT `reg 76.29 the claimant's social insurance number is to be used` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.29 the claimant's social insurance number is to be used` FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 76.3 the Canada Revenue Agency and the Minister of National Revenue are authorized to disclose the information to the province` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.3 the Canada Revenue Agency and the Minister of National Revenue are authorized to disclose the information to the province` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.3 the Canada Revenue Agency and the Minister of National Revenue are authorized to disclose the information to the province` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 76.3 the Canada Revenue Agency and the Minister of National Revenue are authorized to disclose the information to the province` TRUE TRUE FALSE
